{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8gEphvsao3HYrExFy6B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've committed the WI-912 verdict as `fd0ae94a2` with the `WI: WI-912` trailer, and the commit checks passed. As this new protocol asks, I took no act. Flips and snapshots are for the later act turn.\n\n| Section | Machine line | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| `## amendment` | `VERDICT: MEANING rows=10` | All ten rows tagged `[MEANING+BLESS]` |\n| `## first-approval` | `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=2` | LLR-338 and TC-368 approved |\n\nI checked the file with the kit's own readers. The sitting parser accepts it under the combined binding. `blessed_rows` returns exactly the ten amendment rows, and the first-approval rulings read LLR-338 and TC-368 as APPROVE.\n\n**What changed:** the lane splits adjudication into a judging turn and a later act turn.\n- **LLR-167, TC-161 and TC-308:** judging briefs no longer order the act or derive approval tokens.\n- **LLR-306, TC-321 and SR-231:** the coordinator entry point gains an act turn. It only acts on an accepted, committed verdict, reserves no verdict, and succeeds only when every authorized act is taken and no verdict record has changed.\n- **LLR-310:** adds the `[MEANING+BLESS]` tag. Every reader sees it as MEANING, and a row tagged both ways counts as not blessed.\n- **LLR-305, TC-322 and TC-192:** cover the new act brief, which retained sessions now include in their identity and which is a shipped prompt.\n- **LLR-338 and TC-368 (new):** the act assembler. It derives exactly the authorized acts, lists amendment before first approval, handles retirements, and refuses ambiguous states by name.\n\n**Why I blessed and approved:** every new arm traces to SR-231's amended acceptance or SR-232's per-kind scope. Every cited test exists, and all 26 code symbols of LLR-338 resolve. TC-321's move to `Full` is honest because it now cites a slow-only module, and `check_trajectory.py --strict` is clean.\n\n**Three advisories in the verdict, none blocking:**\n1. **Stray back-link:** two act functions tag SR-146, which isn't among LLR-338's parents. Either drop the tag or add SR-146 to the row's SR-Refs.\n2. **Indicative sentences in SR-231:** the new sentences (\"it takes only an act…\") sit outside the row's one `shall`. WI-913's D-008 precedent would fold them in as a second predicate.\n3. **Unclear \"it\" in LLR-167:** \"a released-rung MEANING verdict it blesses\" should name the adjudicator.\n\nThe untracked `.requested` binding file is the coordinator's, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1143,"cache_read_input_tokens":772421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1143},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"e29dd6c9-1795-4bdb-ad74-bbc80b95e501","timestamp":"2026-10-17T23:28:47.449Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8gEpRZBLQ6GrPAt3A4u"}
